  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m meticulously dissecting the user\'s requirements now, aiming for absolute precision. I want to build a financial screener that\'s crystal clear and delivers on every detail, much like a classic, high-density Taiwanese stock screener, but of course with modern features. I\'m focusing on ensuring complete accuracy and crispness in the output.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the data structure, ensuring it aligns perfectly with the user\'s need for a standalone JSON array (`stocksData`) for daily updates. I\'m prioritizing seamless integration with the Python script, making sure the initial 12 sample stocks cover various sectors for comprehensive testing. The plan is to have a robust `public/stocks.json` file.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Management**\n\nI\'m expanding the data management strategy now. I\'m focusing on providing both direct access at `/stocks.json` via Vite (for both development and build), and a fallback `stocksData` array in `src/data/stocksData.ts`. This dual approach will allow seamless Python script updates and direct inspection, plus a user-friendly interface for uploading or refreshing JSON data, keeping the main UI clean. I\'m also planning an info panel for data format explanations and local JSON uploads.\n\n\n\n**Defining Filter Criteria**\n\nI\'m now defining the filter criteria. I\'ve got a detailed list, including dividend yield, dividend frequency, earnings multiples, and director holdings. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness by designing options like a dropdown for ex-dividend months and clear \'Apply Filter\', \'Clear Conditions\', and \'Export CSV\' buttons. I need to make the live filter option, versus \"apply filter\" button, work well in practice, and think hard about the UX, as this is important.\n\n\n**Integrating Filter Behaviors**\n\nI\'m now integrating filter behaviors, aiming for intuitive user interaction.  I\'m focusing on the interplay between real-time keyword search and the \"Apply Filter\" button for numeric/month criteria. The plan is to make \"Apply Filter\" the primary button, include a \"conditions changed\" indicator when necessary, and enable `Enter` key functionality. I\'m also exploring a quick preset strip with interactive buttons for common stock strategies.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Table**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the data table with 23 columns, as per user specification, now. I need to ensure that the order and content are accurate, and include the exact specifications, such as the special display of high dividend yield values. The `code` and `name` columns will be sticky on the left. I\'m taking the Taiwan stock screener, with a \346\222\277\350\202\241\350\256\232 focus, into consideration.\n\n\n**Finalizing Data Table Columns**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final data table columns based on user specifications. I\'m focusing on the display format for percentage values (e.g., `%`), including columns for ex-dividend dates, payout ratios, insider holdings, and average dividends. I need to make sure the average dividend and EPS are correct. I\'m also ensuring sticky headers and left columns for easy navigation, including fixed widths for the code and name columns.\n\n\n**Designing Table Functionality**\n\nI\'m now designing the table\'s functionality, focusing on user interaction and data presentation. I\'m prioritizing clickable column headers that toggle between ascending and descending sort, and are clearly marked. I need to ensure proper sorting logic for numeric and date columns, with null values always at the bottom.\n\n\n**Implementing Table Sorting**\n\nI\'m now implementing the table\'s sort functions. I need to get the sort functions right for numeric and date columns, and especially text columns. I\'m focusing on the `\344\273\243\350\231\237` and `\345\205\254\345\217\270` columns, and I\'ve got to make them work correctly. I will be using `localeCompare` with `zh-Hant-TW` for company names and standard string or numeric comparison for ticker codes.\n\n\n**Evaluating Stock Data**\n\nI\'m now evaluating new stock data, focusing on calculating vital financial metrics. I\'m checking each company\'s price, dividends (cash and stock), dividend yields, ex-dividend dates, and payout ratios. I also need to ensure EPS and insider holdings are correct for a solid foundation.\n\n\n**Calculating Financial Metrics**\n\nI\'m now carefully calculating financial metrics for specific stocks, including price, dividends, yields, and payout ratios. I\'m focused on accuracy, making sure all data aligns with the latest company reports. I\'m double-checking EPS and insider holdings, and making sure the `avgDiv` figures are correct, too. I\'m cross-referencing values and checking for inconsistencies.\n\n\n**Verifying Dividend Data**\n\nI\'m now deeply involved in verifying dividend data for stocks 2884 and 2412, cross-checking cash dividends, stock dividends, and ex-dividend dates to ensure accuracy. I\'m focusing on the `avgDiv` figures, making sure those calculations are correct and consistent with past performance. I\'m double-checking the P/E and P/B ratios, and also the EPS figures.\n\n\n\n**Validating Stock Data**\n\nI\'m now carefully validating the stock data for accuracy. I\'m focusing on the calculations and specific data points, such as the P/E and P/B ratios, and also the EPS figures. The goal is to ensure the calculated financial metrics are accurate, using the latest company reports to cross-reference and check for inconsistencies in each data set.\n\n\n\n**Diversifying Data Points**\n\nI\'m now diversifying the data points. I need to ensure a good mix of ex-dividend months across the 12 entries (April to August). I\'m also ensuring a selection of stocks with cash yields over 5% to make sure the data is representative of a range of strategies.\n\n\n**Calculating Total Yields**\n\nI\'m now calculating total yields, accounting for both cash and stock dividends for accuracy. I\'m focusing on the standard Taiwanese convention used in \346\222\277\350\202\241\350\256\232 and similar platforms. I need to make sure I get the total yield calculation right, especially when stock dividends are involved, such as with \345\205\206\350\261\220\351\207\221, to be accurate.\n\n\n**Refining Color and Layout**\n\nI\'m now refining the color scheme and layout. I\'ve chosen a crisp off-white canvas and a subtle cool blue-slate for structure, with deep navy-slate accents, maintaining the classic Taiwanese financial portal aesthetic. I\'m focusing on high density, clear typography and a clean, user-friendly interface. I will be incorporating zebra-striped table rows.\n\n\n\n**Enhancing Visual Appeal**\n\nI\'m now focusing on visual enhancements. I\'ve set a clean color scheme of off-white and cool blue-slate, with deep navy-slate accents for structure. I\'m prioritizing the high-density aesthetic with clear typography, especially tabular numerals for numbers. I\'ve also incorporated zebra-striped rows, and I will be using semantic data highlighting for important values.\n\n\n**Designing Interface Sections**\n\nI\'m now designing the interface sections, starting with a clean brand title and concise navigation. I\'m focusing on a single-page screener, with navigation links for key views. I\'m incorporating a CSV export button and a panel for filter options. The goal is to design a clean, user-friendly, and informative interface, and to give users direct access to JSON info.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m focusing on the layout\'s three zones. I\'ve got a single-line brand title (`\346\222\277\350\202\241\347\257\251\351\201\270`) in Zone 1. Zone 2 will have clean navigation links like `\346\256\226\345\210\251\347\216\207\347\270\275\350\241\250` and `\350\263\207\346\226\231\346\233\264\346\226\260\350\252\252\346\230\216`, that smoothly interact with the workspace. Zone 3 will include a primary `\345\214\257\345\207\272 CSV` action button, strategically placed near the filter panel. I\'m also planning a slide-over/modal explaining the JSON data schema.\n\n\n**Implementing JSON Loading**\n\nI\'m now implementing JSON loading, focusing on user testability. I plan to allow users to load their own Python-generated `stocks.json` within the browser, and the filter panel action bar needs to include `\345\245\227\347\224\250\347\257\251\351\201\270`, `\346\270\205\351\231\244\346\242\235\344\273\266`, and `\345\214\257\345\207\272\347\233\256\345\211\215\347\265\220\346\236\234\347\202\272 CSV`.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m ensuring the CSV export includes a UTF-8 BOM (`\\uFEFF`) to prevent garbled text in Excel. I\'ll export currently filtered and sorted rows in the correct 23-column order, with the filename `\345\217\260\350\202\241\346\256\226\345\210\251\347\216\207\347\257\251\351\201\270_YYYYMMDD.csv`. I\'m working on loading skeletons for the table and also designing states for empty and error conditions. An inline summary will be displayed right above the table.\n\n\n**Finalizing App Metadata**\n\nI\'m now finalizing metadata updates and syncing HTML details, ensuring a consistent user experience. I\'m focusing on setting the correct language, descriptions, and fonts for optimal presentation. I\'m double-checking the Google Fonts, too.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m also setting up the file structure precisely. I\'m organizing files for metadata, HTML, CSS (Tailwind, font variables, and scrollbars), and TypeScript interfaces. I\'ll include stock data, column definitions, export utilities, and preset strategies. Also, I\'ll ensure the public JSON file works, and I\'m ensuring everything is organized for user testability.\n\n\n**Defining App Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the app\'s core components for a smooth user experience. I\'m building `/src/App.tsx`, for general structure, and also `/src/components/FilterPanel.tsx` and `/src/components/StockTable.tsx`. I\'ll also add a `/src/components/DataGuideModal.tsx` for quick info.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "EwkAa67FG__SjMcPlO7ooA8"
