    thinking: "**Designing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focused on the UI components themselves, starting with `FilterPanel.tsx`. I envision a clean, compact design with a subtle border and minimal elevation to enhance user experience, and I\'m using Tailwind\'s utility classes. I\'m thinking about the layout structure within the panel now.\n\n\n**Refining Filter Inputs**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the filter input components. I\'ve designed a keyword search input with an immediate filter. Also, I\'m working on the design of interactive quick-preset buttons. Moreover, I\'m structuring a main filter grid for various numerical and month-based selections.\n\n\n**Finalizing Stock Table Actions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the action buttons within the filter panel. I\'ve designed the button suite and the button-group: a bold primary button for applying filter conditions; a secondary, bordered button for resetting the filter; and a third to export the current data. I\'ve ensured a strong visual contrast and clear action calls-to-action for each button. I\'m also ensuring the export function will produce UTF-8 BOM CSV output.\n\nFinally, I\'m working to render the exact 23 stock table columns in the exact order. I\'m taking the above actions in a crisp manner. The first two columns are sticky, to allow smooth horizontal scrolling. I\'m also adding a bold highlight to any data that meets or exceeds the 5% dividend yield threshold.\n\n\n**Enhancing Table Column Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on visually refining the table columns. I\'ve added a distinct visual style for data exceeding the 5% dividend yield, using bold text, a red color, and a subtle background for emphasis. Also, I\'m working to make the header cells sticky and interactive for sorting, including accessible keyboard controls and clear visual indicators for sort direction and active columns. The header cells are now clickable and will show either \342\226\262 or \342\226\274 to show ascending or descending order.\n\n\n**Improving Table Rendering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on further table refinements. I\'ve implemented a height of 38px for each row, with crisp zebra striping using `bg-white` and `bg-[#F8FAFC]`. Hover row highlights (`hover:bg-[#EFF6FF]`) enhance user interaction. Sticky left cells, like \'\344\273\243\350\231\237\' and \'\345\205\254\345\217\270\', now carefully inherit matching opaque background colors, ensuring a consistent visual experience during horizontal scrolling. I\'m also adding loading skeleton rows and an empty state, complete with a clear explanation and a `\346\270\205\351\231\244\346\242\235\344\273\266` button.\n\n\n\n**Structuring App Top Bar**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to the application\'s top bar, focusing on a clean three-zone design within `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve settled on the following layout. The first zone will feature a single-line wordmark, `\345\217\260\350\202\241\346\256\226\345\210\251\347\216\207\347\257\251\351\201\270`. The second zone will house navigation links: `\346\256\226\345\210\251\347\216\207\345\244\247\350\241\250`, `\351\253\230\346\201\257 5%+`, `10\345\271\264\345\255\230\350\202\241`, and `\350\263\207\346\226\231\346\233\264\346\226\260\350\252\252\346\230\216`, each directly wired to an action. The third zone will include a primary action button, `\350\274\211\345\205\245 JSON`, for triggering file/JSON modal or a quick reload. I\'m also planning the main widescreen workspace structure, including the `FilterPanel`, a summary strip, and the `StockTable`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "qAkAa-LHE_WU_uMPou25iQ0"
    tool_calls {
